# Laravel Backend Rules

## Models (`app/Models/`)

- Extend `Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model`
- Use traits: `HasFactory`, `SoftDeletes` (on main entities)
- Always define `protected $fillable = [...]` — never use `$guarded`
- Define `casts()` method for JSON/array/datetime fields
- Auto-generate UUID and slug in `boot()` via `static::creating()` callback
- Use `$appends` for computed display attributes (e.g. image URLs)
- Override `getRouteKeyName()` to return `'slug'` or `'uuid'` as appropriate
- Define explicit return types on relationships: `BelongsTo`, `HasMany`, `BelongsToMany`, `HasOne`
- Current models: User, Workspace, Project, Board, BoardColumn, Item, ItemType, ItemPriority, ItemLink, Label, Comment, Attachment, Page, Bookmark, BookmarkItem, ActivityLog, InstanceAdmin, InstanceSettings, WorkspaceInvitation

### Example Model Pattern

```php
class Example extends Model
{
    use HasFactory, SoftDeletes;

    protected $fillable = ['uuid', 'name', 'slug', ...];

    protected function casts(): array
    {
        return ['settings' => 'array', 'is_public' => 'boolean'];
    }

    protected static function boot(): void
    {
        parent::boot();
        static::creating(function ($model) {
            $model->uuid ??= (string) Str::uuid();
            $model->slug ??= Str::slug($model->name);
        });
    }

    public function getRouteKeyName(): string
    {
        return 'slug';
    }
}
```

## Controllers (`app/Http/Controllers/`)

- Extend base `Controller`
- Use `$this->authorize('ability', $model)` for policy checks
- Use inline `$request->validate([...])` for validation
- Return Inertia responses: `Inertia::render('Page/Name', ['prop' => $data])`
- Use eager loading to avoid N+1: `->with(['relation.nested'])` or closure-based eager loading
- Redirects: `redirect()->route('name')` or `back()`
- Flash messages: `session()->flash('success', 'Message')`
- For file uploads: store on `public` disk with UUID filenames
- Scoped routes: use workspace slug → project slug → board slug nesting

## Authorization (Policies)

- Policies in `app/Policies/` — one per main model
- Instance admins bypass all checks (configured via `Gate::before()` in `AppServiceProvider`)
- Policy methods: `viewAny`, `view`, `create`, `update`, `delete`, plus custom (`manageMembers`, `inviteMembers`, etc.)
- Check workspace/project role via `$user->workspaceRole($workspace)` and `$user->projectRole($project)`
- Roles hierarchy: owner > admin > editor > viewer

## Routes (`routes/web.php`)

- Public pages: `/`, `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/cookies`
- Auth group: `middleware(['auth', 'verified'])`
- Nested resource routes scoped by workspace slug and project slug
- Use Ziggy named routes (`->name('routename')`) — all routes must be named

## Migrations

- Use `$table->uuid('uuid')->unique()` on every main model
- Use `$table->string('slug')->unique()` where applicable
- Use `$table->softDeletes()` on main entities
- Use `$table->foreignId('...')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete()` for foreign keys

## Testing

- PHPUnit 11 with `tests/Feature/` and `tests/Unit/`
- Testing DB: SQLite in-memory (`:memory:`)
- Use `RefreshDatabase` trait in feature tests
- Use `actingAs($user)` for authenticated tests
